ru's problem goes far beyond the  former president check this out  [Music]  the political Titanic that is Peru  after three no confidence processes in  just 16 months and while Pedro Castile  will be prosecuted for rebellion and  perhaps also for conspiracy Peru has a  new president Dinah bulatare Castillo's  vice president resigned after the coup  attempt and was very clear in condemning  her former political partner there has  been an attempted coup d'etat an imprint  promoted by Mr Pedro Castillo which is  not found an echo in the institutions of  democracy or in the street this Congress  of the Republic following the  Constitutional mandate has made a  decision and it is my duty to act  accordingly Dina bulata vice president  of Pedro Castillo and the new president  of Peru the new president has asked  Parliament for a political truce and is  promised to establish a government of  national unity in which all political  forces are represented this has  apparently been well received by the  political groups this is not a time for  ideologies neither of left or right  President boluate we wish you success in  forming a government of national Unity  kaiko fujimori but what can I say it is  almost certain that the new president  will again have practically the same  problem as Castile had including an  investigation for money laundering her  problems may even we end up being worse  because her profile is much more  ideological and much more to the left  [Music]  however Peru's problem was not  exclusively castillos but above all the  persistent political catastrophe the  country is experiencing bulutari as the  sixth president the country has had in  the last five years Congress has  practically refused to work loyally with  any of the country's past presence and  take note because if there is one thing  Congress is doing it is monopolizing  more and more power to the point that  the executive is becoming an irrelevant  player practically a punching bag in  fact one 